---
import BaseLayout from '~/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Disclosure from '~/components/Disclosure.astro';
import PageHeader from '~/components/PageHeader.astro';
import Section from '~/components/Section.astro';

import { REVIEW_MODE } from '~/config/compliance';
import { LEGAL_ENTITY } from '~/config/site';

/*
  Antonio's shorter fair housing statement, November 2026. His four sections
  replace the six that were here, and the page keeps its own URL and footer
  link rather than being folded into the privacy policy or the terms, which
  is what he asked for.

  Two things his version leaves out, recorded here because they went on
  purpose and not by accident:

  1. The named list of protected classes is now prose rather than the
     VA_PROTECTED_CLASSES array, and "pregnancy, childbirth or related
     medical conditions" is the one entry that does not appear by name. His
     sentence closes with "or any other characteristic protected by
     applicable law", which covers it, but every other class is named.

  2. The reporting route is gone - the old page named the Virginia Fair
     Housing Office and HUD and linked to both. A reader who believes they
     were treated unfairly now has no onward route from this page.

  Both are flagged for him. VA_PROTECTED_CLASSES and EQUAL_HOUSING_FULL stay
  in compliance.ts: nothing else renders them today, but they are the
  verified source if either comes back.
*/
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Fair Housing & Equal Opportunity"
  description="Our commitment to equal housing opportunity, and to fair and consistent practices in marketing, screening, leasing and management."
>
  <PageHeader
    eyebrow="Fair housing"
    title="Fair Housing &amp; Equal Opportunity"
    lead="We do business in accordance with federal and Virginia fair housing law."
  />

  <Section>
    <div class="prose-site">
      {
        REVIEW_MODE && (
          <Disclosure label="Pre-launch notice" pending>
            <p>
              This statement has not yet been reviewed by a Virginia attorney
              or the supervising broker, and the characteristics listed below
              have not been verified against the current statute. Confirm
              both before launch.
            </p>
          </Disclosure>
        )
      }

      <h2>Our Commitment</h2>
      <p>
        {LEGAL_ENTITY} is committed to providing equal housing opportunities
        and conducting business in accordance with all applicable federal,
        state, and local fair housing laws.
      </p>
      <p>
        We believe everyone deserves to be treated with fairness, dignity, and
        respect throughout the housing process.
      </p>

      <h2>Equal Housing Opportunity</h2>
      <p>
        We support the principles of equal housing opportunity and do not
        discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, national origin,
        sex, disability, familial status, elderliness, source of funds, sexual
        orientation, gender identity, military status, or any other
        characteristic protected by applicable law.
      </p>

      <h2>Fair &amp; Consistent Practices</h2>
      <p>
        We are committed to fair and consistent practices in property
        marketing, applicant screening, leasing, and property management.
      </p>
      <p>
        Rental applications are evaluated using objective, consistently
        applied screening criteria in accordance with applicable fair housing
        requirements.
      </p>
      <p>
        We also recognize the importance of reasonable accommodations and
        modifications for individuals with disabilities, as required by law.
      </p>

      <h2>Our Philosophy</h2>
      <p>
        Fairness, professionalism, and respect are fundamental to how we serve
        property owners, residents, and prospective tenants.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Section>
</BaseLayout>
